page.evaluate can't use setTimeout? It can — `page.evaluate(async () => { await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 1000)); ... })` works fine.

```ts
async function avgCharSpeed(page: Page, ms: number): Promise<number> {
  return page.evaluate((ms) => {
    return new Promise((resolve) => {
      let sum = 0;
      let n = 0;
      const start = Date.now();
      const tick = () => {
        const v = window.__CHAR__?.vel;
        if (v) {
          sum += Math.hypot(v.x, v.z);
          n++;
        }
        if (Date.now() - start >= ms) {
          resolve(n > 0 ? sum / n : -1);
        } else {
          setTimeout(tick, 50);
        }
      };
      tick();
    });
  }, ms);
}
```

Angle between two unit XZ vectors:
```ts
const angleBetween = (a: Vec3, b: Vec3): number => {
  const cross = a.x * b.z - a.z * b.x;
  const dot = a.x * b.x + a.z * b.z;
  return Math.abs(Math.atan2(cross, dot));
};
```

